ponse following exposure to a mild stressor that is disproportionate to the magnitude of the stressor. Hormesis triggers a vast array of protective mechanisms that not only repair cell damage but also provide protection from subsequent exposures to more devastating stressors… The physiological responses to sauna use are remarkably similar to those experienced during moderate- to vigorous-intensity exercise. In fact, sauna use has been proposed as an alternative to exercise for people who are unable to engage in physical activity due to chronic disease or physical limitations.[13]\n\nBased on the article, which of the following statements is the author likely to agree with?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sauna use can prevent the onset of dementia in all cases.\nB. Sauna use is beneficial for mental health regardless of other lifestyle factors.\nC. Patients on a diet would benefit from sauna use.\nD. Patients with skin conditions may be cured with sauna use.\nE. Sauna use may increase the risk of heart disease.\nF. Salt restriction would be equal to sauna use for hypertensive patients.\nG. Heart surgery patients who cannot run on treadmills may benefit from sauna use.\nH. Frequent sauna use causes a significant loss of body weight.\nI. Sauna use can be a potential treatment for Alzheimer's disease.\nJ. Sauna use can completely replace the need for exercise.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}\n\nThe article suggests that sauna use can serve as an alternative to exercise for individuals unable to engage in physical activity due to chronic disease or physical limitations. This aligns with the potential benefits for heart surgery patients who may be physically restricted from activities like running.",
