      "generated_answer": "The best method to assess fetal damage in a diabetic mother in the first trimester is **glycosylated Hb**, as it reflects average blood glucose control over the preceding 2–3 months, which is critical for early fetal development. Other options like blood sugar (snapshot only), urine ketones (not specific for fetal damage), or amniocentesis (invasive and not typically used for sugar measurement) are less suitable.  \n\n\\boxed{D}",
