    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Cost-effectiveness analysis compares costs to outcomes in natural units (e.g., time saved, labour output), making it suitable for assessing outcome from labour, cost, and time together.  \nCost-benefit analysis converts outcomes to monetary values, while cost-utility uses quality-adjusted life years, and risk-benefit focuses on trade-offs of risks and benefits.  \nTherefore, the best match for the given context is cost-effectiveness.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{B}",
