      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}  \nYes, homocysteine levels were significantly higher in vitiligo patients compared to controls (21.61 ± 13.28 vs. 13.1 ± 4.88 μmol/L; *P* < 0.001). Levels were also elevated in active/progressive disease and varied by sex. These findings support a likely relationship between hyperhomocysteinemia and vitiligo pathogenesis.",
