    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}  \nThe study found that individuals with higher financial assets were more likely to accept preventive home visits, indicating a social imbalance. Although the association weakened after adjusting for invitational procedures, differences in acceptance based on socioeconomic status remained evident. This suggests that social inequalities influence participation in the programme.",
      "success": true,
