      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}  \nYes, the study shows that IADL disability significantly predicts dementia at both 1-year (OR = 2.20, 95% CI = 1.51–3.13) and 2-year (OR = 2.11, 95% CI = 1.33–3.33) follow-ups, after adjusting for conventional clinical measures. A higher conversion rate was observed in those with baseline IADL disabilities (24.4% vs. 16.7%), and SEM confirmed its predictive value beyond age, sex, education, depression, and cognitive scores.",
