    "global index": "MusicTheoryBench_202",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following time signatures is a compound meter?\n\nOptions: \nA. 11/8\nB. 7/4\nC. 8/8\nD. 12/16\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**Compound meters** have beats subdivided into three equal parts, typically with the top number being a multiple of 3 (like 6, 9, or 12) when counting eighth or sixteenth notes.  \nAmong the options, **12/16** has 4 beats per measure (each beat is a dotted eighth note subdivided into three sixteenths), fitting the definition of a compound meter.  \nThe others are either irregular (11/8, 7/4) or simple/ambiguous (8/8 is often simple quadruple).\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}",
