      "generated_answer": "The king imposes a trial in the form of a public arena where the accused must choose between two doors. One door leads to a fierce tiger that will kill him as punishment for his guilt, while the other door leads to a lady, whom he must marry as a reward for his innocence. This method of trial reflects the king’s belief in poetic justice shaped by chance. \n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{A trial by chance involving two doors, one leading to death by a tiger and the other to a marriage with a lady.}",
