      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\). In the Supreme Court case Dred Scott v. Sanford (1857), the Court ruled that African Americans, whether free or enslaved, could not be American citizens and thus were not entitled to the rights and privileges of citizenship, directly contradicting Garrison's argument. This decision reinforced the invidious distinction based on race that Garrison argued against.",
