      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    it = iter(data)\n    \n    N = int(next(it)); M = int(next(it))\n    \n    # Build adjacency list and use union-find to track connected components\n    parent = list(range(N + 1))\n    rank = [0] * (N + 1)\n    \n    def find(x):\n        if parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = find(parent[x])\n        return parent[x]\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\n            parent[rx] = ry\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n        else:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n            rank[rx] += 1\n        return True\n    \n    # Process M edges\n    adj = [[] for _ in range(N + 1)]\n    for _ in range(M):\n        u = int(next(it)); v = int(next(it))\n        if u != v:  # skip self-loops for union-find\n            union(u, v)\n        # keep adjacency list for BFS\n        adj[u].append(v)\n        adj[v].append(u)\n    \n    # Read K forbidden pairs\n    K = int(next(it))\n    bad_pairs = []\n    for _ in range(K):\n        x = int(next(it)); y = int(next(it))\n        bad_pairs.append((x, y))\n    \n    # For each node, store its component id\n    comp_id = {}\n    comp_counter = 0\n    visited = [False] * (N + 1)\n    \n    # BFS to assign component IDs\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        if not visited[i]:\n            comp_counter += 1\n            q = deque([i])\n            visited[i] = True\n            while q:\n                cur = q.popleft()\n                comp_id[cur] = comp_counter\n                for neighbor in adj[cur]:\n                    if not visited[neighbor]:\n                        visited[neighbor] = True\n                        q.append(neighbor)\n    \n    # Now process queries\n    Q = int(next(it))\n    res = []\n    for _ in range(Q):\n        p = int(next(it)); q = int(next(it))\n        \n        # Check if adding edge (p,q) connects any bad pair\n        # For each bad pair (x,y), if adding edge (p,q) creates a path between x and y,\n        # then x and y must be in components that become connected via the new edge.\n        # Specifically, if x and y were in different components but now connected via p-q,\n        # meaning: x connected to p, y connected to q OR x connected to q, y connected to p\n        \n        # Since we only care if ANY bad pair becomes connected, we can check for each bad pair\n        # But K and Q can be up to 2e5, so O(K*Q) is too slow.\n        # Instead, we precompute: for each component, store the set of bad pairs it's involved in?\n        # Alternative approach:\n        \n        # Observation: Adding edge (p,q) merges components comp_id[p] and comp_id[q].\n        # So any bad pair (x,y) where x is in comp_id[p], y in comp_id[q] OR vice versa will become connected.\n        # So we need to check: does there exist a bad pair (x,y) such that \n        # {comp_id[x], comp_id[y]} == {comp_id[p], comp_id[q]}\n        # BUT also if x and y were already connected in one component, they remain connected.\n        # However, the original graph was good, so no bad pair (x,y) is connected in G.\n        # So for each bad pair (x,y), comp_id[x] != comp_id[y] originally.\n        # After adding edge between p and q, if comp_id[p] == comp_id[q], nothing changes -> still good for this pair.\n        # If comp_id[p] != comp_id[q], then the two components merge. A bad pair (x,y) becomes connected iff\n        # one of x,y is in comp_id[p] and the other in comp_id[q] (since before, they were in different components).\n        \n        # So for each query (p,q):\n        #   if comp_id[p] == comp_id[q]: adding edge does nothing -> still good -> Yes\n        #   else: we need to check if there exists any bad pair (x,y) such that \n        #         (comp_id[x] == comp_id[p] and comp_id[y] == comp_id[q]) or (comp_id[x] == comp_id[q] and comp_id[y] == comp_id[p])\n        \n        # Precompute a mapping: for each unordered pair of components (c1,c2) (with c1 < c2), \n        # whether there's a bad pair with endpoints in those components.\n        # But number of component pairs could be large.\n        \n        # Alternative: for each bad pair (x,y), record the pair (min(c1,c2), max(c1,c2)).\n        # Then for query (p,q): get c_p = comp_id[p], c_q = comp_id[q]. If c_p == c_q: yes.\n        # Else let key = (min(c_p, c_q), max(c_p, c_q)). Check if key in bad_component_pairs set.\n        \n        # Build bad_component_pairs set once\n        # But note: multiple bad pairs might map to same component pair, that's fine.\n        \n        # Let's do that precomputation here:\n        # Actually we haven't done it yet. We'll build the set now.\n        # But since we're inside main() and haven't built it, let's build it.\n        \n    # Let's refactor: first build component component mapping and bad_component_pairs set.\n    # We'll restructure the code:\n    \n    # Reset variables\n    parent = list(range(N + 1))\n    rank = [0] * (N + 1)\n    \n    def find(x):\n        if parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = find(parent[x])\n        return parent[x]\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\n            parent[rx] = ry\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n        else:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n            rank[rx] += 1\n        return True\n    \n    # Clear adj list\n    adj = [[] for _ in range(N + 1)]\n    for _ in range(M):\n        u = int(next(it)); v = int(next(it))\n        if u != v:\n            union(u, v)\n        adj[u].append(v)\n        adj[v].append(u)\n    \n    # Get component IDs via BFS (using adj)\n    visited = [False] * (N + 1)\n    comp_id = [0] * (N + 1)\n    comp_counter = 0\n    comp_map = {}  # comp_id number -> actual id? no, we'll use the representative as component id\n    \n    # We can use parent array's root as component id\n    # But after unions, we want to compress paths.\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        find(i)\n    \n    comp_to_index = {}\n    comp_index = 0\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        r = parent[i]\n        if r not in comp_to_index:\n            comp_to_index[r] = comp_index\n            comp_index += 1\n        comp_id[i] = comp_to_index[r]\n    \n    # Read K\n    K = int(next(it))\n    bad_pairs = []\n    bad_comp_set = set()\n    for _ in range(K):\n        x = int(next(it)); y = int(next(it))\n        cx, cy = comp_id[x], comp_id[y]\n        if cx != cy:\n            bad_comp_set.add((min(cx, cy), max(cx, cy)))\n    \n    # Read Q\n    Q = int(next(it))\n    for _ in range(Q):\n        p = int(next(it)); q = int(next(it))\n        cp = comp_id[p]\n        cq = comp_id[q]\n        if cp == cq:\n            res.append(\"Yes\")\n        else:\n            key = (min(cp, cq), max(cp, cq))\n            if key in bad_comp_set:\n                res.append(\"No\")\n            else:\n                res.append(\"Yes\")\n    \n    print(\"\\n\".join(res))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
