    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    index = 2\n    edges = []\n    \n    for _ in range(m):\n        k = int(data[index])\n        c = int(data[index + 1])\n        index += 2\n        vertices = list(map(int, data[index:index + k]))\n        index += k\n        \n        # Add all pairs (u, v) with u < v in this subset\n        for i in range(k):\n            for j in range(i + 1, k):\n                u, v = vertices[i], vertices[j]\n                edges.append((c, u, v))\n    \n    # Remove duplicate edges, keeping the one with minimum weight\n    edge_dict = {}\n    for c, u, v in edges:\n        key = (min(u, v), max(u, v))\n        if key not in edge_dict or edge_dict[key] > c:\n            edge_dict[key] = c\n    \n    edges = [(c, u, v) for (u, v), c in edge_dict.items()]\n    \n    # Sort edges by weight for Kruskal's algorithm\n    edges.sort()\n    \n    parent = list(range(n + 1))\n    rank = [0] * (n + 1)\n    \n    def find(x):\n        if parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = find(parent[x])\n        return parent[x]\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        px, py = find(x), find(y)\n        if px == py:\n            return False\n        if rank[px] < rank[py]:\n            px, py = py, px\n        parent[py] = px\n        if rank[px] == rank[py]:\n            rank[px] += 1\n        return True\n    \n    total_weight = 0\n    edge_count = 0\n    \n    for c, u, v in edges:\n        if union(u, v):\n            total_weight += c\n            edge_count += 1\n            if edge_count == n - 1:\n                break\n    \n    if edge_count == n - 1:\n        print(total_weight)\n    else:\n        print(-1)\n\nmain()\n```",
