      "generated_answer": "Here is an executable Python function that implements the solution based on the provided problem statement. It reads input from standard input as specified, constructs the graph based on the operations, and then determines if the graph is connected. If connected, it computes the total weight of the edges in a minimum spanning tree (MST) using Kruskal's algorithm.\n\n```python\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    from heapq import heappop, heappush\n\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().splitlines()\n    \n    # Read N and M\n    N, M = map(int, data[0].split())\n    \n    edges = []\n    \n    index = 1\n    for _ in range(M):\n        K, C = map(int, data[index].split())\n        vertices = list(map(int, data[index + 1].split()))\n        index += 2\n        \n        # Create edges for the complete graph formed by these vertices\n        for i in range(K):\n            for j in range(i + 1, K):\n                edges.append((C, vertices[i], vertices[j]))\n\n    # Function to find the root of an element\n    def find(parent, x):\n        if parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = find(parent, parent[x])\n        return parent[x]\n\n    # Function to union two sets\n    def union(parent, rank, x, y):\n        root_x = find(parent, x)\n        root_y = find(parent, y)\n        if root_x != root_y:\n            if rank[root_x] > rank[root_y]:\n                parent[root_y] = root_x\n            elif rank[root_x] < rank[root_y]:\n                parent[root_x] = root_y\n            else:\n                parent[root_y] = root_x\n                rank[root_x] += 1\n\n    # Kruskal's algorithm to find the MST weight\n    edges.sort()\n    parent = [i for i in range(N + 1)]\n    rank = [0] * (N + 1)\n\n    total_weight = 0\n    edges_used = 0\n\n    for weight, u, v in edges:\n        if find(parent, u) != find(parent, v):\n            union(parent, rank, u, v)\n            total_weight += weight\n            edges_used += 1\n\n    # Check if all vertices are connected\n    root = find(parent, 1)\n    if all(find(parent, i) == root for i in range(1, N + 1)):\n        print(total_weight)\n    else:\n        print(-1)\n\n# Call the main function\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n### How the Code Works:\n1. **Input Handling**: It reads all input at once and splits it into lines for processing.\n2. **Edge Creation**: For each operation that defines a set of vertices and a corresponding weight, the function generates edges between all pairs of vertices and appends them to a list.\n3. **Union-Find Structure**: This structure is implemented to help efficiently manage and unite different components during the MST creation process.\n4. **Kruskal's Algorithm**: It sorts all the generated edges by their weights and applies the union-find structure to build the MST while ensuring that cycles are not created.\n5. **Final Check**: After processing all edges, it checks if all vertices belong to the same connected component. If so, it outputs the total weight of the MST; otherwise, it emits `-1`.\n\nYou can run this function in a Python environment, providing input in the expected format.",
