    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Here is the executable Python function based on the prompt provided. This function reads multiple test cases from standard input, processes them, and prints the maximum absolute difference between the total weights of any two trucks for each test case.\n\n```python\ndef max_truck_weight_difference():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().splitlines()\n    \n    t = int(data[0])  # Read number of test cases\n    results = []\n    index = 1\n    \n    for _ in range(t):\n        n = int(data[index])  # Read number of boxes\n        a = list(map(int, data[index + 1].split()))  # Read the weights of the boxes\n        \n        # We sort the weights\n        a.sort()\n        \n        # The maximum difference will be the difference between the largest\n        # sum of boxes of one truck and the smallest sum of boxes of another\n        max_difference = a[-1] - a[0]\n        \n        results.append(max_difference)\n        index += 2\n    \n    print('\\n'.join(map(str, results)))\n\n# Call the function\nmax_truck_weight_difference()\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n1. **Input Handling**: The input is read all at once using `sys.stdin.read()`, which is efficient for large inputs. The input is then split into lines and processed.\n2. **Loop through Test Cases**: For each test case, the number of boxes `n` is read along with their corresponding weights.\n3. **Processing each Case**:\n   - The weights are sorted to easily access the minimum and maximum weights.\n   - The maximum absolute difference is calculated as `max(a) - min(a)` which is simply the difference between the largest and smallest weights in the sorted list.\n4. **Output**: Finally, the results for each test case are printed in sequence.\n\nThis code is structured to be efficient and straightforward, adhering to the constraints provided in the prompt.",
