    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    # Read Team Takahashi's scores for the top of innings 1-9\n    A = list(map(int, input().split()))\n    \n    # Read Team Aoki's scores for the bottom of innings 1-8\n    B = list(map(int, input().split()))\n    \n    # Calculate total runs for each team\n    takahashi_total = sum(A)  # Runs from top of innings 1-9\n    aoki_current = sum(B)    # Runs from bottom of innings 1-8\n    \n    # Team Aoki needs to score enough runs in the bottom of the 9th to have strictly more than Team Takahashi\n    # So they need at least (takahashi_total - aoki_current + 1) runs\n    runs_needed = takahashi_total - aoki_current + 1\n    \n    # If the result is negative or zero, they need at least 1 run to win\n    # But since Takahashi's total >= Aoki's current total (given constraint), \n    # runs_needed will always be at least 1 when they're tied, or positive when behind\n    print(max(1, runs_needed))\n\nsolve()\n```",
