    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict, deque\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    events = []\n    index = 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        t = int(data[index]); x = int(data[index+1]); index += 2\n        events.append((t, x))\n    \n    # Count future monster requirements per type\n    future_monsters = defaultdict(int)\n    for t, x in events:\n        if t == 2:\n            future_monsters[x] += 1\n    \n    # We'll simulate the events and decide whether to pick up potion or not\n    potions_held = defaultdict(int)\n    max_potions = 0\n    current_potions_count = 0\n    pickup_actions = []  # To record decisions for t=1 events\n    \n    # We need to know which events are potion events\n    potion_event_indices = []\n    for i, (t, x) in enumerate(events):\n        if t == 1:\n            potion_event_indices.append(i)\n    \n    # For each potion event, we decide whether to pick it up\n    # First, simulate with greedy optimal strategy to find minimum K_min\n    # We can use binary search on K (maximum potions held at any time)\n    \n    def can_succeed(max_allowed_potions):\n        pot = defaultdict(int)\n        count = 0\n        monsters_left = future_monsters.copy()\n        \n        for t, x in events:\n            if t == 1:\n                # Decide whether to pick up\n                if count < max_allowed_potions:\n                    # Pick it up\n                    pot[x] += 1\n                    count += 1\n                else:\n                    # Cannot pick up\n                    pass\n            else: # t == 2 (monster)\n                if pot[x] > 0:\n                    pot[x] -= 1\n                    count -= 1\n                else:\n                    return False\n        return True\n\n    # Binary search on K_min\n    low, high = 0, n\n    K_min = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if can_succeed(mid):\n            K_min = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        else:\n            low = mid + 1\n    \n    if K_min == -1:\n        print(-1)\n        return\n\n    # Now reconstruct one valid strategy that uses at most K_min potions simultaneously\n    potions = defaultdict(int)\n    current_count = 0\n    actions = []\n    monsters_remaining = future_monsters.copy()\n    \n    event_idx = 0\n    for t, x in events:\n        if t == 1:\n            if current_count < K_min:\n                # Pick up\n                potions[x] += 1\n                current_count += 1\n                actions.append(1)\n            else:\n                # Skip\n                actions.append(0)\n        else: # t == 2\n            if potions[x] > 0:\n                potions[x] -= 1\n                current_count -= 1\n            else:\n                # Should not happen if our binary search was correct\n                print(-1)\n                return\n        event_idx += 1\n    \n    print(K_min)\n    print(\" \".join(map(str, actions)))\n\nsolve()\n```",
