      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve() -> None:\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    it = iter(data)\n    N = int(next(it))\n    M = int(next(it))\n    L = [int(next(it)) for _ in range(N)]\n\n    # Minimum possible width is the largest word\n    low = max(L)\n    # Maximum possible width is all words in one line with spaces\n    high = sum(L) + (N - 1)\n\n    def feasible(W: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Check whether we can fit all words into at most M lines with width <= W.\"\"\"\n        if N == 0:   # edge case (not in constraints but safe)\n            return True\n        lines = 1\n        current = L[0]               # width of current line without trailing space\n        for i in range(1, N):\n            # if we can add the next word with a space before it\n            if current + 1 + L[i] <= W:\n                current += 1 + L[i]\n            else:\n                lines += 1\n                current = L[i]\n                if lines > M:\n                    return False\n        return lines <= M\n\n    lo, hi = low, high\n    while lo < hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if feasible(mid):\n            hi = mid\n        else:\n            lo = mid + 1\n    print(lo)\n```",
