      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque, defaultdict\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    it = iter(data)\n    N = int(next(it))\n    M = int(next(it))\n    parent = [0] * (N + 1)\n    for i in range(2, N + 1):\n        parent[i] = int(next(it))\n    \n    # Build tree structure\n    children = [[] for _ in range(N + 1)]\n    for i in range(2, N + 1):\n        children[parent[i]].append(i)\n    \n    # Read insurance events\n    insurances = []\n    for _ in range(M):\n        x = int(next(it))\n        y = int(next(it))\n        insurances.append((x, y))\n    \n    # BFS to compute max coverage depth for each node\n    max_depth = [-1] * (N + 1)  # max_depth[i]: farthest generation covered for node i\n    \n    for x, y in insurances:\n        if y > max_depth[x]:\n            max_depth[x] = y\n    \n    # Propagate coverage downward using BFS\n    q = deque([i for i in range(1, N + 1) if max_depth[i] >= 0])\n    visited = [False] * (N + 1)\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        if max_depth[i] >= 0:\n            visited[i] = True\n    \n    while q:\n        u = q.popleft()\n        if max_depth[u] <= 0:\n            continue\n        for v in children[u]:\n            if max_depth[v] < max_depth[u] - 1:\n                max_depth[v] = max_depth[u] - 1\n                if not visited[v]:\n                    visited[v] = True\n                    q.append(v)\n    \n    # Count covered people\n    count = sum(1 for i in range(1, N + 1) if visited[i])\n    print(count)\n\nsolve()\n```",
