      "generated_answer": "Here's the Python function that solves the given problem:\n\n```python\ndef sumOfPower(nums, k):\n    n = len(nums)\n    nums.sort()\n    result = 0\n    mod = 10 ** 9 + 7\n\n    for i in range(n - k + 1):\n        min_diff = float('inf')\n        for j in range(i, i + k):\n            min_diff = min(min_diff, abs(nums[j] - nums[i]))\n        result = (result + min_diff) % mod\n\n    return result\n```\n\nThis function takes in the array `nums` and the integer `k`, and returns the sum of powers of all subsequences of `nums` which have length equal to `k`, modulo `10^9 + 7`.\n\nThe key steps are:\n\n1. Sort the input array `nums` in ascending order.\n2. Iterate through the array from index `i` to `i + k - 1`, and for each such subsequence, calculate the minimum absolute difference between any two elements in the subsequence.\n3. Add this minimum difference to the `result` variable, and take the result modulo `10^9 + 7` to avoid overflow.\n4. Return the final `result`.\n\nNote that this function does not invoke itself, it only defines the function body.",
