    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minGroupsForValidAssignment(nums):\n    from collections import Counter\n    \n    # Count frequency of each value\n    freq_count = Counter(nums)\n    frequencies = list(freq_count.values())\n    \n    # Try different numbers of groups\n    n = len(nums)\n    \n    # The minimum number of groups is at least the number of distinct values\n    # The maximum number of groups is n (each index in its own group)\n    \n    def can_assign(groups):\n        # For a given number of groups, check if we can assign indices\n        # such that the difference in group sizes is at most 1\n        total_indices = n\n        base_size = total_indices // groups\n        larger_groups = total_indices % groups  # number of groups with size = base_size + 1\n        smaller_groups = groups - larger_groups  # number of groups with size = base_size\n        \n        # We need to assign frequencies to groups\n        # Each group can only contain indices with the same value\n        # So we need to split each frequency across groups\n        \n        # For each distinct value, we need to distribute its frequency across groups\n        # We want to minimize the number of groups used, so we try to fill groups optimally\n        \n        # For a frequency f, we need to split it into group_size chunks\n        # where group_size is either base_size or base_size + 1\n        \n        # The minimum number of groups needed for a frequency f is ceil(f / (base_size + 1))\n        # But we also need to make sure we don't exceed the available groups\n        \n        total_required = 0\n        max_per_large = base_size + 1\n        max_per_small = base_size\n        \n        for freq in frequencies:\n            # We need to split this frequency across groups\n            # We want to use as few groups as possible, so we try to put as many as possible in each group\n            # Each group can hold at most max_per_large elements\n            \n            # The minimum number of groups needed for this frequency\n            min_groups_for_freq = (freq + max_per_large - 1) // max_per_large\n            total_required += min_groups_for_freq\n            \n        return total_required <= groups\n    \n    # Binary search on the number of groups\n    left, right = 1, n\n    result = n\n    \n    while left <= right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        if can_assign(mid):\n            result = mid\n            right = mid - 1\n        else:\n            left = mid + 1\n    \n    return result\n```",
